<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Home-screen "Frequency Cassette" widget (renamed 2026-09-10, direct user request — was
     "Soundtrack") — plays the app's own ambient "Log Screen" music tracks (the same 4
     choices as Profile > Display > Sound > Ambient Music: 1.0/2.0/3.0 Login Screen +
     Convene) via SoundtrackPlaybackService, a genuine foreground MediaPlayer service so
     playback survives the widget/app not being on screen.

     Restyled to use the user's own product photo (public/widgets/cassette-widget.png,
     alpha-cutout around the device's own irregular silhouette, decoded by
     SoundtrackWidget.java) rather than a hand-drawn reinterpretation — see that class's own
     header for why decodeAsset + this file's scaleType="fitXY" (not fitCenter/centerCrop) is
     required for the fractional overlay positions below to track the photo's real button
     positions at any widget size.

     Track name text and the transport controls are positioned as FRACTIONS of the photo's
     own measured pixel layout (currently a 1858×1017 source: the blank cream panel inside
     the tape-reel window at x 725-1580/y 417-519 for text; the 4 physical button labels at
     x 613-1552/y 824-957 for controls; the yellow diagram panel at roughly x 204-501/
     y 224-596 for the shuffle toggle), built from nested weighted LinearLayouts (RemoteViews
     has no percentage-margin attribute, so weight-sum spacers are the standard substitute).
     Re-measured and the button mapping corrected 2026-09-10 per direct user review of a
     debug overlay image (see PHASE/commit history — this is the SECOND numeric pass; the
     first pass's positions were confirmed accurate by the same overlay method, but its
     button-to-action mapping was wrong) — the real mapping, left to right on the 4 physical
     buttons: Prev, Next, Loop, Play/Stop. Shuffle didn't fit anywhere in that row and was
     moved into the middle of the yellow diagram panel on the left instead, per the user's
     own direction.

     Icon rendering fix (same day, direct user report of "glitched or invisible" button
     icons): every control below except Play/Stop now renders NO icon at all — just an
     invisible tap zone over the photo's own already-printed button face, plus the existing
     selected-overlay tint for Loop/Shuffle's on/off state. Root cause: a button's weighted
     cell height is a FRACTION OF THE WIDGET'S OWN HEIGHT (~13% for the button row), and
     since home-screen widgets are typically wide-and-short (e.g. a 3×2-cell placement is
     roughly 250×110dp), that fraction can collapse to under 15dp tall — an icon with
     scaleType="fitCenter" inside a cell that short scales down to near-nothing, which is
     what "invisible" was. Play/Stop is the one control that genuinely needs a live icon (it
     has to show playing vs paused, which the static photo can't), so it keeps one — but
     wrapped in its own FIXED-size inner box (22dp square, gravity="center") instead of
     filling the outer weighted cell directly, so its aspect ratio can never collapse no
     matter how short that outer cell gets.

     The root background is genuinely transparent (@android:color/transparent) — the photo's
     own alpha cutout is the widget's real visible edge.

     TWO alternate content blocks — widget_soundtrack_content_normal (the photo-mapped
     layout above) reads fine down to 2 cells tall, but doesn't fit in a 1-cell-tall
     placement at all (the photo would be squeezed into an unrecognizable sliver);
     widget_soundtrack_content_compact falls back to a plain flat row — text + small FIXED-dp
     icon buttons (not weighted, so they don't have this same squish problem at all) — which
     SoundtrackWidget.java switches to below its own height threshold, same compact-mode
     pattern PulseBannerWidget.java already uses. Both blocks' data/PendingIntents are
     applied identically every render; only whichever one is actually visible matters.

     No plain <View> anywhere (RemoteViews' allowlist doesn't include it) — spacer/positioner
     layers use empty FrameLayouts instead. -->
<FrameLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:background="@android:color/transparent">

    <ImageView
        android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_bg_art"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="match_parent"
        android:scaleType="fitXY"
        android:contentDescription="@null" />

    <!-- ═══ Normal (>= 2 cells tall): photo-position-mapped overlay ═══ -->
    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_content_normal"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="match_parent"
        android:orientation="vertical">

        <!-- Row 1/3 — track name. Re-measured 2026-09-10 directly against a real-device
             screenshot (not just the source photo) after a user report that the title
             rendered cut/overlapping the reel art: pixel-scanning that screenshot for the
             actual dark-text row found "Convene" sitting at ~24-33% of the widget's height,
             not the 41-51% these weights previously computed from the source photo's blank
             panel alone — that photo-only measurement never actually confirmed where the
             TextView renders relative to the widget's real total height, only that the panel
             existed at that fraction of the photo.

             Second real-device round (same day): the vertical position landed correctly, but
             every glyph was sliced clean across the top — a DIFFERENT bug. A weighted 0dp-height
             row is a HARD cell: LinearLayout's default clipChildren=true clips a wrap_content
             child taller than that cell. Fixed with clipChildren="false" on this row and the
             text's own wrapper as a safety net against a cell shorter than the text.

             Third real-device round (same day): text was no longer clipped, but the user
             pointed out a legible flat white panel just below the reel graphic (the one this
             text was sitting ON TOP of) and asked for the title there instead. That round's fix
             was fit from a SCREENSHOT again (65/10/25) — the same category of mistake as the
             very first round: that particular screenshot included status-bar chrome above the
             actual widget bounds, so treating the whole screenshot as 0-100% of the widget
             squeezed/shifted every fraction, and the user reported the title still not on the
             white space.

             Fourth round: went back to the SOURCE PHOTO itself (not a screenshot of it, which
             can include chrome outside the widget's real bounds) and pixel-scanned it directly
             for the actual white drawer panel below the reel window — a distinctly brighter
             white than the cream panel above it, at y 72-84% / x 47-81% of the 1858x1017
             photo. That panel's bottom (84%) overlaps the button row's own top (81%, see Row
             2/3 below) — only y 72-81% (9%) is actually clear of both the cream panel above and
             the button row below. The second round's fix used an 18%-tall cell to stop 14sp
             bold text from clipping; 18% doesn't fit in a 9%-tall clear band. Rather than
             re-risk clipping by cramming a too-short cell in again, dropped the text to 12sp
             (still bold, still legible, needs a shorter cell to render without clipping) and
             sized the cell to the clear band itself: 73/8/19 vertical, 47/34/19 horizontal
             (horizontal unchanged from the panel measurement — only the vertical band was
             ever the problem).

             Fifth round: that "white drawer panel" the fourth round found was actually the
             thin DIAGONAL scrub-bar ledge, not a real flat panel — a rectangular weighted box
             can never cleanly fit a tapering diagonal shape, which is why every attempt to
             land fully on it kept overhanging onto the reel art or the button row. The real
             flat panel is the bigger rectangular slab directly ABOVE that ledge (it has its
             own faint printed placeholder microtext near its top, visible in the source
             photo) — found by rendering candidate boxes directly onto the source photo and
             checking them against it, not by re-deriving fractions from another screenshot.
             Confirmed edges via sharp seam/color-transition scans on the real photo: panel
             spans x 38.2-86.65% / y 41.3-69.8%. Final box sits in the clear area below that
             panel's own microtext and is centered on the panel's true seam-measured center
             (62.4% horizontal) rather than an approximate one: 52/13/35 vertical, 39/47/14
             horizontal.

             Sixth round: the source photo (public/widgets/cassette-widget.png) grew a real
             offset drop-shadow around its left/bottom edge (direct user request, "impression
             de profondeur") — the device art's own pixel content is UNCHANGED, but it now
             sits inset by a 96px pad on every side of a larger 2050x1017->1209 canvas (was
             1858x1017) instead of filling it edge to edge, so every fraction below that was
             measured against the OLD canvas needed exact recomputation, not a re-guess: for
             each cumulative weight boundary c (0..wsum), f_old=c/wsum,
             f_new=(96 + f_old*old_dim)/new_dim, c_new=f_new*wsum — then consecutive
             differences become the new weights, with a new leading/trailing pad-spacer child
             added at each group's own start/end (weight ~16 vertical / ~5 horizontal, from
             96/new_dim*wsum) to represent the new inset itself. Applied identically to every
             weight-group in this file (title row here, the button row and shuffle group
             further down) — see PullBubbleService... no, see the actual computation: this
             was a script, not hand math, specifically to avoid yet another mis-measured
             round on a widget that's already had five. -->
        <!-- CORRECTED 2026-09-10: content_normal's direct vertical children were flattened
             into ONE shared weightSum (Android sums all sibling weights when unset) —
             52+13+35+81+13+6 = 200, not 100 — silently halving every intended percentage
             below 50% and roughly doubling every one above it ever since round one. The
             title and button rows were meant to each get their own scoped 100%, and
             instead shared 200, which is why real renders never actually matched the
             comments' stated percentages despite looking "close enough" to pass on a real
             device. Verified by rendering candidate boxes onto the actual photo: the buggy
             weights land nowhere near the real buttons/title panel; these corrected ones
             (single flat list, genuinely summing to 100: 8/44/11/13/11/5/8) land exactly on
             both. -->
        <FrameLayout
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:layout_weight="8" />
        <FrameLayout
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:layout_weight="44" />
        <LinearLayout
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:layout_weight="11"
            android:orientation="horizontal"
            android:clipChildren="false">
            <FrameLayout
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_weight="5" />
            <FrameLayout
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_weight="35" />
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_track_name"
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_weight="42"
                android:gravity="center"
                android:background="@drawable/widget_title_backing_black25"
                android:clipChildren="false">
                <!-- ellipsize/marqueeRepeatLimit/focusable* below are the NATIVE Android
                     marquee attempt — direct user request ("both") alongside the manual
                     ticker SoundtrackWidget.buildTickerText() actually drives. Real marquee
                     only animates once a view has focus, which a home-screen widget host
                     never grants, so this is expected to sit inert in practice; it's free to
                     leave in and does nothing if it doesn't fire. -->
                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_track_name_text"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:textColor="#3D2817"
                    android:textSize="12sp"
                    android:singleLine="true"
                    android:ellipsize="marquee"
                    android:marqueeRepeatLimit="marquee_forever"
                    android:focusable="true"
                    android:focusableInTouchMode="true"
                    android:textStyle="bold"
                    android:maxLines="1" />
            </LinearLayout>
            <FrameLayout
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_weight="13" />
            <FrameLayout
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_weight="5" />
        </LinearLayout>
        <FrameLayout
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:layout_weight="13" />

        <!-- Row 2/3 — the 4 real physical button labels, horizontal weights
             5/29/10/11/13/12/15/5 (was 33/11/12/14/13/17, remapped for the shadow canvas
             per this file's earlier comment; verified against real pixel translation).
             Left to right: Prev, Next, Loop, Play/Stop. Vertical position is this single
             LinearLayout's own weight=11 within content_normal's now-CORRECTED flat
             8/44/11/13/11/5/8 (wsum=100) — see that structural fix noted further up. -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:layout_weight="11"
            android:orientation="horizontal">
            <FrameLayout
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_weight="5" />
            <FrameLayout
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_weight="29" />
            <!-- Every control below uses the SAME fixed-size-icon-box pattern: a real icon in
                 a FIXED dp square (layout_gravity="center"), not filling the outer weighted
                 cell directly. The first icon pass (no icon at all, tap zone only over the
                 photo's own printed — and, on a real device, hard-to-read — button face) fixed
                 the collapse-to-invisible bug but over-corrected into controls with zero visual
                 affordance; a user report of "buttons not visible enough" on 2026-09-10 is the
                 same root cause from the other direction. This is the actual fix: a fixed-size
                 icon can never be squashed by the outer cell's aspect ratio (the original bug),
                 and unlike no icon at all, it's still visible against the photo. -->
            <FrameLayout
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_weight="10">
                <ImageButton
                    android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_prev"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="match_parent"
                    android:background="@android:color/transparent"
                    android:contentDescription="@string/widget_soundtrack_prev_aria" />
                <ImageView
                    android:layout_width="18dp"
                    android:layout_height="18dp"
                    android:layout_gravity="center"
                    android:translationX="1dp"
                    android:translationY="2dp"
                    android:src="@android:drawable/ic_media_previous"
                    android:tint="#3D2817"
                    android:contentDescription="@null" />
            </FrameLayout>
            <FrameLayout
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_weight="11">
                <ImageButton
                    android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_next"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="match_parent"
                    android:background="@android:color/transparent"
                    android:contentDescription="@string/widget_soundtrack_next_aria" />
                <ImageView
                    android:layout_width="18dp"
                    android:layout_height="18dp"
                    android:layout_gravity="center"
                    android:translationX="1dp"
                    android:translationY="2dp"
                    android:src="@android:drawable/ic_media_next"
                    android:tint="#3D2817"
                    android:contentDescription="@null" />
            </FrameLayout>
            <!-- Loop toggle. Selected-state overlay: RemoteViews can't runtime-swap a view's
                 own background, so the "on" highlight is a second view toggled by visibility,
                 layered under the fixed-size icon above. -->
            <FrameLayout
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_weight="13">
                <FrameLayout
                    android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_loop_selected"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="match_parent"
                    android:background="@drawable/widget_target_selected_emerald"
                    android:visibility="gone" />
                <ImageButton
                    android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_loop"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="match_parent"
                    android:background="@android:color/transparent"
                    android:contentDescription="@string/widget_soundtrack_loop_aria" />
                <ImageView
                    android:layout_width="18dp"
                    android:layout_height="18dp"
                    android:layout_gravity="center"
                    android:translationX="1dp"
                    android:translationY="2dp"
                    android:src="@drawable/ic_loop_widget"
                    android:contentDescription="@null" />
            </FrameLayout>
            <!-- Play/Stop — same fixed-size pattern, now 18dp to match the other three icons
                 (was 22dp/"slightly larger" — direct user request to size it the same). -->
            <FrameLayout
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_weight="12">
                <ImageButton
                    android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_play"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="match_parent"
                    android:background="@android:color/transparent"
                    android:contentDescription="@string/widget_soundtrack_play_aria" />
                <ImageView
                    android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_play_icon"
                    android:layout_width="18dp"
                    android:layout_height="18dp"
                    android:layout_gravity="center"
                    android:translationX="1dp"
                    android:translationY="2dp"
                    android:src="@android:drawable/ic_media_play"
                    android:tint="#3D2817"
                    android:contentDescription="@null" />
            </FrameLayout>
            <FrameLayout
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_weight="15" />
            <FrameLayout
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_weight="5" />
        </LinearLayout>
        <FrameLayout
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:layout_weight="5" />
        <FrameLayout
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:layout_weight="8" />
    </LinearLayout>

    <!-- Shuffle toggle, moved into the middle of the yellow diagram panel on the left
         (horizontal weights 11/16/73 ≈ x 204-501 of 1858; vertical weights 22/37/41 ≈
         y 224-596 of 1017) — per direct user direction (it didn't fit in the 4-button row).
         A SIBLING of widget_soundtrack_content_normal (not nested inside it) since it needs
         its own independent weighted-positioner tree rooted at the full widget height rather
         than the transport row's — SoundtrackWidget.java toggles this id's visibility in
         lockstep with content_normal/content_compact so it doesn't float over the compact
         layout too. Same fixed-size-icon-box pattern as the transport row (see its own
         comment) — a real icon, sized so it can't collapse.

         Sixth-round shadow-canvas remap (see title row's own comment): vertical 8/19/31/34/8
         (was 22/37/41, new leading/trailing 8s for the canvas's own top/bottom inset),
         horizontal 5/10/15/65/5 (was 11/16/73, new leading/trailing 5s). -->
    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_shuffle_dial_wrap"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="match_parent"
        android:orientation="vertical">
        <FrameLayout android:layout_width="match_parent" android:layout_height="0dp" android:layout_weight="8" />
        <FrameLayout android:layout_width="match_parent" android:layout_height="0dp" android:layout_weight="19" />
        <LinearLayout
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:layout_weight="31"
            android:orientation="horizontal">
            <FrameLayout android:layout_width="0dp" android:layout_height="match_parent" android:layout_weight="5" />
            <FrameLayout android:layout_width="0dp" android:layout_height="match_parent" android:layout_weight="10" />
            <FrameLayout
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_weight="15">
                <FrameLayout
                    android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_shuffle_selected"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="match_parent"
                    android:background="@drawable/widget_target_selected_emerald"
                    android:visibility="gone" />
                <ImageButton
                    android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_shuffle"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="match_parent"
                    android:background="@android:color/transparent"
                    android:contentDescription="@string/widget_soundtrack_shuffle_aria" />
                <ImageView
                    android:layout_width="13dp"
                    android:layout_height="13dp"
                    android:layout_gravity="center"
                    android:translationX="-1dp"
                    android:src="@drawable/ic_shuffle_widget"
                    android:contentDescription="@null" />
            </FrameLayout>
            <FrameLayout android:layout_width="0dp" android:layout_height="match_parent" android:layout_weight="65" />
            <FrameLayout android:layout_width="0dp" android:layout_height="match_parent" android:layout_weight="5" />
        </LinearLayout>
        <FrameLayout android:layout_width="match_parent" android:layout_height="0dp" android:layout_weight="34" />
        <FrameLayout android:layout_width="match_parent" android:layout_height="0dp" android:layout_weight="8" />
    </LinearLayout>

    <!-- ═══ Compact (1 cell tall): plain flat row, FIXED-dp icon buttons (no weighted-cell
         squish problem at all — kept as normal icons here) ═══ -->
    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_content_compact"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="match_parent"
        android:orientation="horizontal"
        android:gravity="center_vertical"
        android:paddingLeft="8dp"
        android:paddingRight="8dp"
        android:visibility="gone">

        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_track_name_compact_text"
            android:layout_width="0dp"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_weight="1"
            android:layout_marginRight="6dp"
            android:textColor="#3D2817"
            android:textSize="16sp"
            android:textStyle="bold"
            android:maxLines="1"
            android:ellipsize="end" />

        <FrameLayout
            android:layout_width="24dp"
            android:layout_height="24dp">
            <FrameLayout
                android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_shuffle_selected_compact"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:background="@drawable/widget_target_selected_emerald"
                android:visibility="gone" />
            <ImageButton
                android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_shuffle_compact"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:background="@android:color/transparent"
                android:src="@drawable/ic_shuffle_widget"
                android:scaleType="fitCenter"
                android:padding="2dp"
                android:contentDescription="@string/widget_soundtrack_shuffle_aria" />
        </FrameLayout>

        <ImageButton
            android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_prev_compact"
            android:layout_width="24dp"
            android:layout_height="24dp"
            android:layout_marginLeft="6dp"
            android:background="@android:color/transparent"
            android:src="@android:drawable/ic_media_previous"
            android:tint="#3D2817"
            android:scaleType="fitCenter"
            android:contentDescription="@string/widget_soundtrack_prev_aria" />

        <ImageButton
            android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_play_compact"
            android:layout_width="32dp"
            android:layout_height="32dp"
            android:layout_marginLeft="6dp"
            android:background="@android:color/transparent"
            android:src="@android:drawable/ic_media_play"
            android:tint="#3D2817"
            android:scaleType="fitCenter"
            android:padding="4dp"
            android:contentDescription="@string/widget_soundtrack_play_aria" />

        <ImageButton
            android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_next_compact"
            android:layout_width="24dp"
            android:layout_height="24dp"
            android:layout_marginLeft="6dp"
            android:background="@android:color/transparent"
            android:src="@android:drawable/ic_media_next"
            android:tint="#3D2817"
            android:scaleType="fitCenter"
            android:contentDescription="@string/widget_soundtrack_next_aria" />

        <FrameLayout
            android:layout_width="24dp"
            android:layout_height="24dp"
            android:layout_marginLeft="6dp">
            <FrameLayout
                android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_loop_selected_compact"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:background="@drawable/widget_target_selected_emerald"
                android:visibility="gone" />
            <ImageButton
                android:id="@+id/widget_soundtrack_loop_compact"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:background="@android:color/transparent"
                android:src="@drawable/ic_loop_widget"
                android:scaleType="fitCenter"
                android:padding="2dp"
                android:contentDescription="@string/widget_soundtrack_loop_aria" />
        </FrameLayout>
    </LinearLayout>
</FrameLayout>
